window.MANUAL_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"title": "Manual Overview", "url": "index.html", "category": "Getting Started", "roles": "All users", "snippet": "How this manual is organised and which pages to read for your job.", "keywords": " pages for your job manual sections getting started front of house kitchen &amp; stock money, staff &amp; setup", "text": " how to use this manual every page shows who uses it under the title. find your job in the table below and read only those pages. steps use the exact button names you see on screen, and menu paths are written like sale > pos (menu group, then page). pages for your job your job read these pages cashier / host login & open register , pos: check-in & billing , how to seat & bill a walk-in , reservations , refills , how to close the register chef / kitchen supervisor production & kitchen panel , refills & waste , food menus & recipes storekeeper ingredients, stock & waste , purchases & suppliers accountant payment accounts & accounting , purchases & suppliers , which report do i need? manager / owner dashboard , customers, promotions & loyalty , staff, roles & salary , reports , meal times & prices admin (first-time setup) restaurant setup checklist , settings, tax & white label , equipment & printers manual sections getting started log in, open your register and learn the screen. introduction & key concepts equipment & printers login & open register everyday basics front of house check guests in, print tokens, bill and take bookings. dashboard & live status pos: check-in & billing reservations, cancellations & refunds customers, promotions & loyalty quotations marketing & messaging kitchen & stock cook productions, answer refills, buy and count stock. production & kitchen panel food menus & recipes ingredients, stock & waste purchases & suppliers money, staff & setup accounts, salaries, reports and restaurant settings. payment accounts & accounting accounting reports & ledgers fixed assets staff, roles & salary which report do i need? restaurant setup checklist settings, tax & white label meal times & prices what you see may differ slightly you only see the menus and buttons your role allows. names, prices, tables and dishes in the pictures come from a sample restaurant; yours will be different. "}, {"title": "Introduction & Key Concepts", "url": "01-introduction.html", "category": "Getting Started", "roles": "All users", "snippet": "What Buffet ERP does and how a buffet day runs in it.", "keywords": "per person pricing tokens refill a buffet day in buffet erp the main screen the side menu", "text": " what buffet erp is buffet erp is the software your restaurant uses to take bookings, check guests in, bill them, plan cooking, keep stock, pay suppliers and staff, and keep the accounts. a buffet charges per person (adult, child or senior) for each meal time, not per dish. a buffet day in buffet erp open the register. the cashier logs in and opens (or joins) a register on open register . the pos does not work without one. cook. the kitchen enters a production for the meal time and cooks it on the kitchen panel . check guests in. booked guests are picked from the reservation list; walk-ins start with instant reservation . the cashier checks in the arriving guests and the pos prints food tokens when the meal time uses them. refill. when a dish runs low, the cashier sends a refill request to the kitchen. bill. the cashier clicks generate invoice , takes the payment and clicks settle & close . the money goes into the chosen payment account and the accounts are updated automatically. close. the kitchen marks the meal time done and records leftovers under waste & preserve . the cashier closes the register. screen the main screen after you log in you see the side menu on the left and a top bar with search, notifications, language and your profile picture. the home page shows your profile and the user list. figure 1.1: the home page. the side menu is grouped by department. the side menu menu group what it is for items & stock ingredients, food menus, stock, production and kitchens. sales & customers the pos, sales list, refunds, promotions and customers. reservation add reservations, the reservation list and online reservations. purchase & expense purchases, purchase returns, suppliers, supplier payments and advances, expenses. waste & preserve record food and stock that is thrown away or kept for later. finance & accounting payment accounts, deposits, transfers, accounting and fixed assets. marketing sms, email and whatsapp messages, and quotations. hr management roles, employees, attendance and salary. report all report screens (see which report do i need? ). settings restaurant settings, printers, counters, floors, tables, meal times and prices. "}, {"title": "Equipment & Printers", "url": "02-requirements.html", "category": "Getting Started", "roles": "Owner, Manager", "snippet": "The computers, tablets and printers you need, and how printers are added.", "keywords": "printer thermal network windows equipment for each area adding a printer settings &gt; add printer", "text": " how buffet erp runs buffet erp opens in a web browser (chrome, edge, firefox or safari). nothing has to be installed on each computer or tablet. all devices must be able to reach the restaurant's buffet erp address. equipment for each area area what you need used for cashier counter a computer or a large tablet (the pos screen has three columns, so a wide screen works best). check-in, tokens, billing. receipt / token printer a thermal printer, 56 mm or 80 mm paper. invoices, food tokens, x-report. kitchen a tablet or screen near the cooking area. the kitchen panel and refill requests. kitchen printer (optional) a thermal printer linked to the kitchen. kitchen order tickets (kot). office any computer. reports, purchases, accounts, settings. adding a printer settings settings > add printer enter a printer name that users will recognise (for example \"counter 1 receipts\"). choose the printing choice : browser popup print : the browser's print window opens and you pick the printer. direct print : buffet erp sends the print to the printer. then choose the printer type : network printer (enter the ipv4 address , printer ip address and printer port address , usually 9100) or windows printer (enter the share name of the printer shared on the computer). also enter characters per line (46 for 80 mm paper). choose the printing format : thermal 56mm , thermal 80mm or no auto kot print . set status to active and click submit . figure 2.1: add printer with direct print and network printer selected. printers are then linked where they are used: a counter has an invoice printer and a bill printer , and a kitchen has a printer . see restaurant setup checklist . printer port if you are not sure of the port, print a test page from the printer itself after switching it on. the port is printed on that page. "}, {"title": "Login & Open Register", "url": "03-getting-started.html", "category": "Getting Started", "roles": "All users", "snippet": "Sign in with email or PIN and open or join a register before using the POS.", "keywords": "login pin open register join counter opening balance log in open or join a register start working", "text": " before you start your manager gives you an email and password, or a 6-digit login pin. to use the pos, a counter must already exist ( settings > add counter ). step 1 log in the login page has two tabs: login using email : enter your email and password, tick remember me on your own device only, and click login . login using pin : type your 6-digit pin, one number per box. you are logged in as soon as you type the sixth number. your restaurant may show only one of the two tabs (set in settings > settings , login option ). figure 3.1: the login page. message why what to do \"the provided credentials are incorrect\" the email or password is wrong. check the spelling, or use forgot password? . \"invalid pin\" no user has that pin. re-type it. your manager can see or change your pin on your employee record. step 2 open or join a register go to sale > pos . if you have no open register, you are taken to the open register page. it has two tabs: new register : choose your counter , then type the money you start with in the box for each payment account (for example cash in the drawer under the cash account, 0 for the others). the total opening balance is added up for you. click submit . existing register : a register is already open on that counter (another cashier opened it). choose the counter and click submit to join it. figure 3.2: new register: one opening balance per payment account. figure 3.3: existing register: join a register that is already open. field required? what to enter counter yes the counter you work at. the + button opens add counter. one box per payment account no the money in that account at the start. leave 0 if none. negative numbers are not allowed. if you see \"no active payment account found.\", ask your manager to add one in payment account > add payment account . step 3 start working after the register opens, sale > pos shows your counter name, the current meal time and the floor plan. continue with pos: check-in & billing . at the end of your shift, see how to close the register . "}, {"title": "Everyday Basics", "url": "23-everyday-basics.html", "category": "Getting Started", "roles": "All users", "snippet": "Profile, password, language, light or dark theme, search, filters and export.", "keywords": "password profile language bangla arabic dark mode export pdf excel csv print your profile and password language light or dark screen finding things export and print bulk upload", "text": " your profile and password click your picture at the top right. the menu has change profile , change password , security question and logout . change profile : first name, last name, email, phone and photo ( upload new photo , jpg, gif or png up to 2 mb). click save changes . change password : enter the current password , the new password and confirm password , then submit . generate password suggests a strong one. security question : set the question and answer used by forgot password? on the login page. changing your login pin you cannot change your 6-digit pin yourself. a manager changes it in employee > list employee (edit your record, login pin ). language click the language icon in the top bar and choose english, french, arabic, spanish, portuguese, german or bangla (listed as \"bangeli\"). arabic shows the screen right-to-left. light or dark screen use the theme button in the top bar: light , dark , or system (follows your computer's setting). finding things search (top bar, or ctrl + k ): type a page name to jump to it. list pages have a search box above the table. many also have a filter box: pick values and click submit ; reset filters clears them. show inactive (on some lists) shows records that were switched to inactive. export and print most lists and reports have an export button with export as csv , export as excel , export as pdf and print . reports also have their own print, pdf and excel buttons. bulk upload lists such as ingredients, food menus, customers, suppliers and employees have a bulk upload button. click download sample , fill in the file in the same format, then choose file and submit . if the file has mistakes, the errors are listed; fix the file and upload it again. "}, {"title": "Dashboard & Live Status", "url": "04-dashboard.html", "category": "Front of House", "roles": "Owner, Manager", "snippet": "Read the sales cards, Live Today, Needs attention and the sales trend.", "keywords": "net sales guests served average collections net cash live today choose the period the six summary cards live today and needs attention charts and lists", "text": " before you start open dashboard from the top of the side menu. under the title you see today's date and the meal time that is running. top choose the period the buttons at the top right set the period for the cards and charts: today , yesterday , this week , this month or custom . custom shows date from and date to . cards the six summary cards card what it shows for the chosen period net sales sales from settled bills. guests served number of guests billed. average per guest net sales divided by guests served. collections money received from customers. expenses & purchases money spent on expenses and purchases. lower is better, so a fall shows in green. net cash money in minus money out. the percentage on each card is the change compared with the period before (for example, today compared with yesterday). green is good, red is not. figure 4.1: period buttons and the six summary cards. live live today and needs attention live today counts today's bookings for the running meal time: booked , in house (checked in, still dining), settled , no-show and cancelled . the meal time's guests: how many expected guests have arrived. tables : how many are in use and how many are free. needs attention lists work waiting for someone: refunds pending (with the amount), refill requests waiting and low-stock items . click a line to open that page. figure 4.2: live today, needs attention and the sales trend chart. charts charts and lists sales trend : one point per day of the chosen period. use the net sales and guests buttons to show or hide each line. sales by meal time , collections by payment account and reservation source . upcoming reservations today , recent invoices and low stock , each with view all . figure 4.3: charts and the recent lists further down the dashboard. "}, {"title": "POS: Check-in & Billing", "url": "05-pos-operations.html", "category": "Front of House", "roles": "Cashier", "snippet": "The POS screen: reservations, floor plan, check-in, tokens, invoice and settle.", "keywords": "pos floor check in token invoice settle discount pin split the pos screen three columns and a top bar what the seat colours mean checking guests in select the reservation check in the guests who are here add-ons and stock limits billing generate invoice, take payment, settle &amp; close past invoices: sale &gt; list sale find, view, reprint, and export invoices common messages", "text": " before you start you need an open register. if you have none, sale > pos sends you to open register (see login & open register ). the pos screen screen three columns and a top bar top bar : your counter, the date and meal time, and the buttons refill , shift summary and register . left: reservations. the instant reservation button, the tabs upcoming , in house and settled (and unsettled when a bill from an earlier meal time is still open), and a search by name or number. middle: floor plan of your counter's floor, with how many guests are in, dining, and how many tables are free. right: the selected reservation : check-in, tokens, add-ons, running bill and generate invoice . figure 5.1: the pos screen before a reservation is selected. colours what the seat colours mean available (green) : free seats. selected (yellow) : seats of the reservation you have selected or are choosing tables for. reserved (red) : seats taken by guests who are already checked in. booked (blue) : seats held for a booking whose guests have not arrived yet. tapping a table (outside choose table mode) selects the party seated there; tap again to move to the next party on a shared table. tapping a blue table opens that booking. after a bill is settled the table shows cleaning ; tap it and click mark ready once it has been reset. checking guests in step 1 select the reservation booked guests: pick them in the upcoming tab (or search by name or number). walk-in guests: click instant reservation , enter the customer name and phone number (or search a saved customer), set the adults , children and senior counts with + and −, tick walk-in guest (advance pay optional) if no advance is taken, and click create reservation . the new reservation is selected for you. figure 5.2: instant reservation. discounts and an advance payment can be added here too. step 2 check in the guests who are here in the right panel under guests arriving now , enter how many adults, children and seniors have arrived. you can check guests in a few at a time. optional: click choose table . only in this mode do you tap tables: tap free tables to add or remove them, then set the guests per table in the right panel. cancel leaves the mode. click check in n & print n tokens . if the meal time has no token items, the button is check in n . the tokens window opens: click print n slips , or later . guests who never come: click no show and confirm. the reservation is cancelled and its tables are freed. if an advance was paid, see reservations, cancellations & refunds . more guests than booked: check them in anyway. they are charged at the per-person price. step 3 add-ons and stock limits under add-on food • chargeable , staff can add paid extras (such as bottled drinks or specialty dishes) during the meal: an add-on that is a stock item shows its stock on the card (\"stock: n\", or \"out of stock\"). tap + to add one. you cannot go above the stock: the pos shows only n [unit] of \"[name]\" left in stock , or \"[name]\" is out of stock . click save add-ons . if any of them are token items, click save & print token to print one slip per item. add-ons are added to the bill. lost tokens: click reprint in the check-in history . billing step 4 generate invoice, take payment, settle & close select the party (from in house , or tap their table). the right panel shows the running bill . click generate invoice . the invoice window opens. optional discounts: under discounts & loyalty pick an available one (membership, birthday / anniversary, group discount); or enter a coupon code and click apply ; or enter a manual discount (an amount or a %), the approver's 4-digit pin , and click apply . optional: wastage penalty (number of plates with too much leftover food), and loyalty points to redeem if the customer has enough. under payment , choose split bill ( no split , or 2 ways or more), then for each share pick the payment method and amount. one share can mix methods ( add payment method ). click print bill if the guest wants to check it first, then settle & close . a booking advance already paid is taken off the bill as deposit adjusted . after settling, the party moves to the settled tab, where reprint invoice is available. past invoices: sale > list sale history find, view, reprint, and export invoices to review or reprint past customer bills after they leave the pos screen, go to sale > list sale : search with the box \"search by invoice, reservation or customer\". under sale filter choose the date from , date to , counter, register and meal time, then click submit ( reset filters clears them). the list shows invoice no , date & time , reservation , customer , counter , guests , gross sales , discount , tax , total and status . click the eye icon ( view & reprint ) to see the invoice and its payments , then reprint to print it again. export offers export as csv , export as excel , export as pdf and print . common messages message why what to do only n [unit] of \"[name]\" left in stock / \"[name]\" is out of stock you tried to add more add-on items than available inventory. adjust the quantity to match available stock or replenish stock in inventory. not enough stock for \"[name]\": only n [unit] left. when saving, the stock was already lower (for example another counter sold it first). lower the add-on quantity to the remaining stock balance. \"wrong pin.\" the 4-digit discount pin is not right for that manual discount. ask the approver to type their own pin. after several wrong tries you must wait before trying again. \"this pin allows a discount up to [amount].\" / \"the discount cannot be more than [amount] for this pin.\" the discount is bigger than the limit set on that manual discount. lower the discount, or use a pin of a manual discount with a higher limit. \"share [n] is paid more than its amount. change can only be returned with a cash payment.\" a card, bank or wallet payment is more than the share. enter the exact amount for non-cash payments; give change only on cash. \"no act"}, {"title": "Reservations, Cancellations & Refunds", "url": "06-reservations.html", "category": "Front of House", "roles": "Cashier, Manager", "snippet": "Add a reservation, take an advance, confirm online bookings, cancel and refund.", "keywords": "add reservation advance online cancel no show refund fee add a reservation reservation &gt; add reservation find and change reservations reservation &gt; reservation list edit a reservation what can and cannot change online reservations reservation &gt; online reservations cancellations, no-shows and refunds sale &gt; refund", "text": " before you start meal times with prices and an advance payment amount must exist ( how to set meal times & prices ), and a floor plan must be set up. without a floor plan, add reservation shows \"no floor plan configured. please set up a floor plan in settings first.\" add a reservation step 1 reservation > add reservation check the reservation date and choose the meal time . if a meal time's scheduled dining hours have already passed for today, it is marked with (ended for today) and cannot be chosen. view food menu shows what that meal time serves. choose the customer , or click + to add a new one (customer name and phone number are required). set adult guests , child guests and senior guests . at least 1 guest is needed. under table selection , choose the area/floor and click tables to pick seats until every guest has a seat. green seats are available, yellow are selected, red are already reserved. the booking summary shows the subtotal, discounts (after a customer and meal time are chosen), tax, total amount and minimum amount to pay . take the advance: choose the counter , the payment account and the paid amount ( add payment for a second method). for a walk-in with no advance, tick walk-in guest (advance pay optional) . click submit , or print & save to print the receipt as well. figure 6.1: add reservation. how the minimum advance is worked out: each meal time (and weekend or special day price) has an advance payment amount : either a fixed amount per guest (for example 20) or a percentage of the booking (for example 10%). the total is rounded to a whole amount and is never more than the bill. message what to do \"please select a customer.\" / \"please select a meal time.\" / \"please select a reservation date.\" fill in that field. \"please select at least one table from the floor plan.\" pick tables in table selection. \"please select seats for all n guests (m selected).\" pick more seats until every guest has one. \"this table is fully reserved for the selected date and meal time.\" choose another table. \"please select the counter.\" choose the counter that takes the money. \"collect at least [amount] or mark as walk-in.\" raise the paid amount to the minimum, or tick walk-in guest. find and change reservations list reservation > reservation list search by name, number or reference, or filter by meal time and reservation status . from a row you can view, edit, delete or print receipt . settled and cancelled reservations cannot be edited. figure 6.2: reservation list. to cancel a reservation, edit it and set reservation status to cancelled . the status can be pending, confirmed or cancelled. edit a reservation edit what can and cannot change to adjust a booking before guests arrive, go to reservation > reservation list and click the edit (pencil) icon: what can be changed : reservation date & meal time : you can change the date or move to another active meal time. note: a booking that is already booked for an ended meal time today can keep its own meal time, but you cannot move a booking into a different ended meal time today. customer details : switch or edit the customer assigned to the booking. guest headcounts : increase or decrease adult, child, or senior counts. table assignments : reassign or add seats on the interactive floor plan. notes : update the guest's special requests. promotions & coupons : apply or remove eligible discounts. advance payments : take an additional deposit if guest counts increase. what cannot be changed : cancelled bookings : cancelled reservations are permanently locked ( \"cancelled reservations cannot be edited.\" ). settled bookings : once a booking is checked in and settled at the pos, it cannot be modified here ( \"settled reservations cannot be edited.\" ). deleting a paid booking : a reservation that has received payments cannot be deleted (\"this reservation has received payments in the books, so it cannot be deleted. cancel it instead: the fee is kept and the rest of the advance refunded.\"). cancel it instead; the refund then appears under sale > refund . online reservations online reservation > online reservations guests can book on your public booking page (its link is under website settings > online reservation setting , online reservation link ). the page asks a small sum (for example 7 + 5) to block spam bookings, and can take payment online. on the public online booking page, any meal time whose dining hours have already ended for today shows ended for today and cannot be booked. the tiles show total bookings , pending , confirmed and cancelled . for a pending booking click confirm (or cancel ). only a pending booking can be confirmed or cancelled here. a booking that is not paid within the payment time limit (minutes) becomes expired . if money arrives after that, the filter paid after expiry (refund) shows it so you can refund it. figure 6.3: the public booking page guests see. figure 6.4: online reservations. cancellations, no-shows and refunds refund sale > refund when a booking with an advance is cancelled, or marked no show at the pos, part of the advance can be kept as a fee. the fee is the no-show & cancellation fee in settings > settings (a flat amount, or a % of the booking). the rest is owed back to the guest and appears in sale > refund (and as \"refunds pending\" on the dashboard). open sale > refund . filter by date or status , or search by reservation, customer or phone. open the refund. click pay refund , choose the payment account the money leaves from, and submit. the full amount is paid at once. or click deny refund : the money stays in the account and is recorded as income. this cannot be undone. figure 6.5: refund list with advance paid, fee kept and the refund. "}, {"title": "Customers, Promotions & Loyalty", "url": "19-customers-promotions.html", "category": "Front of House", "roles": "Manager, Cashier", "snippet": "Add customers, set up the six promotion types and loyalty points.", "keywords": "customer coupon membership birthday group manual discount loyalty points customers customer &gt; add customer customer &gt; customer list promotions and discounts promotion &amp; discount &gt; add promotion &amp; discount strict promotion validation rules promotion &amp; discount &gt; list promotion &amp; discount loyalty points turn loyalty points on", "text": " customers add customer > add customer field required? why it matters customer name yes shown on bookings and bills. phone number (with country code) yes 4 to 15 digits. used to find the customer at the pos. email , address , state , notes no state is needed for the tax breakdown when tax is worked out by state. date of birth , anniversary date no needed for the birthday / anniversary discount. cannot be a future date. status yes active or inactive. customers can also be added directly during booking in add reservation or at the pos via instant reservation . list customer > customer list manage your customer database, check contact details, and follow up with diners: customer type : filter the list. the choices are regular and the title of each membership discount you created under promotion & discount . show inactive : click this button to see inactive customers (it then reads show active ). next to each phone number, the phone icon calls the customer and the whatsapp icon opens a whatsapp chat with them. the eye icon opens customer details : name, phone, email, date of birth, anniversary date, address, notes, and who added the customer and when. bulk upload : click bulk upload to import large customer lists from an excel file at once. figure 19.1: add customer. promotions and discounts add promotion & discount > add promotion & discount choose the type , enter a title , the applicable meal time (all meal time by default), the discount (an amount such as 500, or a percentage such as 10%) and the status . the other fields depend on the type: type when it applies extra fields discount everyone, between two dates. start date , end date (required). membership discount regular customers who have visited enough times and spend enough. minimum visit count , minimum bill amount , usage limit (how many times one customer can use it). birthday / anniversary discount on the customer's birthday or anniversary (same day and month). none. the customer needs a date of birth or anniversary date. group discount when one reservation has at least this many guests (adults, seniors and children together). minimum guest count . coupon when the guest gives the code. coupon code (letters, numbers, - and _; saved in capitals), dates, minimum bill amount , usage limit (total uses; empty = unlimited). manual discount when a manager approves it at the pos. the discount here is the maximum discount . add each approver with add user and give them a 4-digit pin ( generate pin makes one). only employees who can log in are listed. figure 19.2: add promotion & discount (type discount). at the pos and in reservations, available discounts appear under discounts & loyalty ; ones that do not apply show why (for example \"needs 5 visits\" or \"no birthday / anniversary today\"). coupons and manual discounts have their own boxes. see pos: check-in & billing . rules strict promotion validation rules when creating or modifying promotions, buffet erp enforces these business rules: end date not in the past : when setting or updating an end date , it cannot be in the past ( \"the end date cannot be in the past.\" ). on edit, an existing expired promotion can keep its past end date if unchanged, but moving it requires today or a future date. flat discount cannot exceed minimum bill : for flat discounts under coupon or membership promotions, the discount value cannot be larger than the minimum bill amount ( \"a flat discount cannot be more than the minimum bill amount.\" ). usage limit cannot be less than existing uses : when editing a coupon, the usage limit cannot be reduced below the number of times it has already been used ( \"this coupon has already been used n times, so the usage limit cannot be less than n.\" ). the form displays used so far: n times for tracking. single use per booking : a promotion is counted only once per booking, whether it was applied in add reservation or at the pos checkout. cancelled/expired bookings release uses : if a customer cancels a booking or an online reservation expires before payment, the promotion use is automatically returned back to the available pool. membership limit is per customer : for a membership promotion, the usage limit specifies how many times each individual customer can benefit from the discount. manage promotion & discount > list promotion & discount search, review, edit, or remove configured promotions and discount cards: filter by type : filter by all types , discount , membership discount , birthday / anniversary discount , manual discount , group discount , or coupon . show inactive : click this button to see inactive promotions (it then reads show active ). search : search promotions instantly by title or coupon code. actions : view details : open the modal to review discount percentage, applicability, meal times, visit limits, and authorized manager pins. edit : modify promotional dates, discount percentages, or add authorized pin users. delete : permanently delete a promotion after confirming the warning dialog (\"are you sure you want to delete this record? this action cannot be undone.\"). loyalty points setup turn loyalty points on in settings > settings set loyalty point to enable , the loyalty point rate (1 point equals how much money) and the minimum loyalty point to redeem . in each meal time set the loyalty point a customer earns when their reservation for that meal time is settled at the pos. earning happens only when a bill is settled at the pos. redeeming : in the invoice window, the loyalty points box shows the customer's balance; enter the points to redeem. at least the minimum must be used at once, no more than the balance, and no more than the amount due. the receipt shows the points earned and the new balance. reports: available loyalty point report and usage loyalty point report . "}, {"title": "Quotations", "url": "26-quotations.html", "category": "Front of House", "roles": "Manager, Cashier", "snippet": "Create, print and manage formal event and group dining price proposals.", "keywords": "quotation estimate proposal banquet catering add a quotation quotation &gt; add quotation find, print and edit quotations quotation &gt; quotation list what happens next common problems", "text": " before you start a quotation is a price offer for a group or event, worked out per guest (adult, senior, child) for one meal time. you do not pick dishes. the customer must exist (or be added with + ), and meal times with prices must be set up. to email a quotation, email settings must be configured. figure 26.1: add quotation with guests entered and the quotation summary. add a quotation add quotation > add quotation field required? what to enter example quotation no. — filled in for you. — customer yes who the offer is for. — date yes the event date. — meal time yes choosing it fills in its per-person prices. dinner guest quantity per guest type at least 1 guest in total how many adult, senior and child guests. 50 adults price per person — filled in from the meal time; you can change it for this offer. — discount no in the quotation summary , next to apply discount : an amount (for example 500) or a percentage (for example 10%). 10% note no conditions or special arrangements. — each row shows its amount (quantity × price per person). the quotation summary shows the subtotal , the discount, tax (only when tax is collected; worked out after the discount) and the grand total . a guest row can be removed with its trash icon; add guest type brings it back. at least one row always stays. then click one of: submit : save. save & email : save and email the quotation to the customer. print & save : save and print. reset clears the form; cancel leaves without saving. find, print and edit quotations list quotation > quotation list columns: sn , quotation no , customer , event date , meal time , total guests , cost per person (adult) , cost per person (senior) , cost per person (child) , added by , added date , actions . the eye icon opens the details ( customer & company , event details , guest & pricing details , cost summary , note ) with a print details button. other actions: download pdf , print , edit, and delete (\"are you sure you want to delete this quotation?\"). what happens next a quotation is only an offer: it does not book tables, take money or change stock. when the customer agrees, make a reservation in reservation > add reservation . the quotation report lists quotations by date. common problems message what to do \"the guest quantity should be at least 1.\" enter at least one guest. \"the discount must be an amount (e.g. 500) or a percentage (e.g. 10%).\" type a number, or a number with %. \"the discount must not exceed the subtotal.\" / \"the discount must not exceed 100%.\" lower the discount. \"email is not configured. please configure email settings first.\" set up settings > email settings , or use submit and print instead. \"quotation saved but email failed.\" the quotation is saved; check the customer's email and the email settings, then try again. "}, {"title": "Marketing & Messaging", "url": "25-marketing.html", "category": "Front of House", "roles": "Manager", "snippet": "Send promotional campaigns, birthday wishes and anniversary greetings via SMS, Email and WhatsApp.", "keywords": "marketing campaign sms email whatsapp birthday anniversary the three marketing screens marketing &gt; sms marketing, email marketing, whatsapp marketing birthday and anniversary messages birthday sms / anniversary sms (and the email and whatsapp versions) custom messages custom sms (and custom email, custom whatsapp) report &gt; marketing report what was sent what happens next common problems", "text": " before you start set up the channel first: settings > sms setting , settings > email settings or settings > whatsapp settings (see restaurant setup checklist ). until then the marketing screen shows, for example, \"please enable and configure sms service provider first.\" birthday and anniversary messages need customers with a date of birth or anniversary date. figure 25.1: sms marketing: the three counters and the birthday sms and anniversary sms cards (here with the provider warning at the top). the three marketing screens screens marketing > sms marketing, email marketing, whatsapp marketing messages are sent only when you click a send button; nothing is sent on a timer. email marketing : there is no subject field. whatsapp marketing sends through the provider chosen in settings > whatsapp settings (twilio or rcsoft). each screen shows three counters: customers with birthday today , customers with anniversary today , and customers with phone (sms and whatsapp) or customers with email (email). birthday and anniversary messages steps birthday sms / anniversary sms (and the email and whatsapp versions) check the message in the birthday sms (or anniversary sms ) card. reload from message templates puts the default greeting back (for example \"hi [customer_full_name], wishing you a happy birthday from …\"). when sending, [customer_full_name] becomes each customer's name, and [restaurant_name] and [branch_name] become your restaurant's name and branch. watch the character count . for sms it shows the count out of 160. the card says who will get it, for example \"this sms will be sent to customers celebrating their birthday today.\" with the total recipients . click send birthday sms or send anniversary sms (email: send birthday email / send anniversary email ; whatsapp: send birthday whatsapp / send anniversary whatsapp ). custom messages steps custom sms (and custom email, custom whatsapp) under recipients , pick customers, or leave it empty to send to everyone (the box says \"select recipients (leave empty to send to all)\"). recipients selected shows how many you picked. write the sms message (or email message / whatsapp message ). click send custom sms (or send custom email / send custom whatsapp ). the confirm send window says \"you are about to send a custom sms to n customers. this action cannot be undone. are you sure you want to proceed?\" click confirm & send , or cancel . reset clears the recipients and the message. whatsapp adds: \"if these numbers do not have whatsapp accounts, the messages will not be sent.\" report > marketing report report what was sent cards: sends , sent , failed , sms , email , whatsapp . filters: date from , date to , channel, type (birthday, anniversary, custom) and status (sent, partly failed, failed). click submit ; reset filters clears them. columns: sn , date , channel , type , recipients , sent , failed , sent on , status , sent by . what happens next each send is recorded in the marketing report with how many messages went out and how many failed. no money or stock changes. common problems message what to do \"please enable and configure sms service provider first.\" (or email / whatsapp) set up the provider in settings, then come back. total recipients is 0 no customer has a birthday or anniversary today, or their dates are not filled in. report status failed or partly failed check the numbers or emails of those customers and the provider settings. "}, {"title": "Production & Kitchen Panel", "url": "07-kitchen-production.html", "category": "Kitchen & Stock", "roles": "Chef", "snippet": "Plan a production, cook it on the kitchen panel and mark the meal time done.", "keywords": "production cooking status meal time status kitchen panel kot plan a production production &gt; production forecast production &gt; add production cook it the kitchen panel set the two statuses in list production production &gt; food menu stock set up a kitchen kitchen &gt; add kitchen", "text": " how production moves stock the app's own guide says it in one line: create production → cooking done (food stock up, ingredients down) → meal time done (food stock down) → record waste & preserve (preserved food back to stock). saving a production does not move any stock by itself. plan a production optional production > production forecast pick a forecast date and meal time and click generate production forecast . it suggests a quantity for each food menu (from past sales, or from the production amounts set on the food menu when there is no sales history) and lists the ingredients to purchase . formula of forecasting explains each number. step 1 production > add production the reference no is filled in for you. check the production date and choose the meal time . choose the food menu items. for each one the table shows food menu in stock ; enter the production qty . need to production is what still has to be cooked after the stock is used. click generate ingredient requirement . the total ingredient requirement lists each ingredient once with the required qty , ingredient in stock and need to purchase . if something is short, go to purchase opens add purchase. click submit , or save draft to finish later. figure 7.1: add production. not enough stock \"you cannot submit this production because the following ingredients are out of stock or not enough stock\" means you must buy or adjust those ingredients first, or lower the quantities. cook it step 2 the kitchen panel open kitchen > list kitchen and click the icon in the panel column of your kitchen. the panel opens in a new tab. it shows the food menus of the categories linked to that kitchen. each item shows not ready , cooking or ready . tick items and tap start cooking or ready , or use start all and ready all . the production and refill request buttons at the top switch views; the number shows refill requests still waiting. new requests play a sound. filter by production date or meal time, and print the list. figure 7.2: the kitchen panel, production view. step 3 set the two statuses in list production in production > list production each production has a cooking status (pending, cooking, done) and a meal time status . cooking status = done : the ingredients are taken out of stock and the cooked quantity is added to food menu stock . meal time status = done (after the meal time ends): the served quantities are taken out of food menu stock. this cannot be undone. then the add waste & preserve button appears so you can record the leftovers (see how to request refills & log waste ). from the list you can also check kitchen panel and print kot (the kitchen order ticket with the items for that kitchen). the guide button explains the workflow. figure 7.3: list production. stock production > food menu stock shows how much of each cooked food menu is in stock, with low stock items and out of stock items . it shows the last production date of each food menu. set up a kitchen setup kitchen > add kitchen enter the kitchen name , choose a printer , tick the food menu categories this kitchen cooks, set the status and click submit . a category can belong to only one kitchen, so categories already given to another kitchen are not listed. a food menu goes to the kitchen of its category; if its category has no kitchen, it cannot be sent as a refill request. "}, {"title": "Food Menus & Recipes", "url": "08-menus-recipes.html", "category": "Kitchen & Stock", "roles": "Manager, Chef", "snippet": "Add food menus with ingredients, production amounts, token, add-on and refill options.", "keywords": "food menu category recipe tokenized add-on refillable add a food menu items &gt; add food menu: name and recipe meal times, production amounts and options find and sort food menus items &gt; list food menu items &gt; food menu item sorting common messages", "text": " before you start add the ingredients first ( items > add ingredient/item ), a food menu category ( items > add food menu category ; all categories are in items > list food menu category ) and the meal times ( settings > add meal time ). add a food menu step 1 items > add food menu: name and recipe enter the code , name and optional alternative name and description . choose the category (the + button adds a new one). note: the food menu name must be unique across the entire restaurant. if you enter an existing name on add or edit, the system alerts: \"a food menu with this name already exists.\" under add ingredient , search each ingredient and enter the consumption (in the unit shown). the unit cost and total are filled in; total ingredient cost , other cost and total food cost are added up below. figure 8.1: add food menu, name and ingredients. step 2 meal times, production amounts and options field required? meaning applicable for yes the meal times this dish is served at ( select all for all). production unit yes the unit the kitchen cooks in (for example portion). + adds a unit. production amount for meal times yes, more than 0 how much is usually cooked for each meal time. used by the production forecast. production amount for weekend days / special days when set up the same, for weekend days and special days. tokenized food yes (yes/no) yes = the pos prints a food token for each guest at check-in. add-on item yes (yes/no) yes = it can be sold as a paid extra at the pos. then enter the add-on price (more than 0). is refillable? yes (yes/no) yes = the cashier can send a refill request for it. image no jpg, png or webp. you can crop it, or click generate to find one. status yes active or inactive. click submit . missing fields show messages such as \"the tokenized food is required.\" or \"the production amount is required and must be greater than 0.\" figure 8.2: applicable for, production amounts and the yes/no options. find and sort food menus list items > list food menu food menus are shown as cards with the image, category, cost and code. filter by category , meal time , tokenized food , add-on item and refillable , then apply filters . bulk upload adds many food menus from a file. if any row in your upload sheet contains a name that is already in use, the import halts with the error: \"a food menu named \"[dish name]\" already exists.\" figure 8.3: list food menu. order items > food menu item sorting choose a meal time to see its food menus, then drag them into the order you want. figure 8.4: food menu item sorting before a meal time is chosen. common messages message why it happens what to do \"a food menu with this name already exists.\" you tried to save a food menu with a name already used by another dish. change the dish name to be unique (e.g. add a portion or style suffix like \"chicken biryani (spicy)\"). \"a food menu named \"[name]\" already exists.\" a spreadsheet row in bulk upload has a duplicate dish name. check and rename duplicate dish names in the excel file before re-uploading. \"the tokenized food is required.\" / \"the production amount is required and must be greater than 0.\" a mandatory field was left empty or 0. complete the missing options or production quantities. "}, {"title": "Ingredients, Stock & Waste", "url": "09-inventory-stock.html", "category": "Kitchen & Stock", "roles": "Storekeeper", "snippet": "Ingredients, stock, low stock, stock adjustment and waste & preserve.", "keywords": "ingredient stock low stock adjustment waste preserve ingredients and items items &gt; add ingredient/item stock stock &gt; ingredient stock and low stock stock &gt; add stock adjustment waste &amp; preserve waste &amp; preserve &gt; add waste &amp; preserve common messages", "text": " ingredients and items setup items > add ingredient/item choose the type : ingredient (used in recipes) or item (something you sell or use as it is). then fill in: field meaning name , code , category how the ingredient is found. categories are added in items > add ingredient category . purchase unit the unit you buy in (for example kg). consumption unit and conversion rate the unit the kitchen uses (for example g), and how many of them make one purchase unit (1000). for an item this is the sale unit . cost per unit / purchase price what it costs. stock alert qty below this the ingredient shows in low stock. minimum purchase qty purchase forecasting never suggests buying less than this. opening stock how much you have when you start. units are added in items > add ingredient unit and listed in items > list ingredient unit ; categories are in items > list ingredient category . many ingredients can be added at once with bulk upload on list ingredient/item . figure 9.1: list ingredient/item. stock check stock > ingredient stock and low stock ingredient stock shows the stock of every ingredient. low stock lists only those at or below their stock alert qty , with tiles for the number of low items, their value and the items that are out of stock. figure 9.2: low stock. correct stock > add stock adjustment use this when the counted stock differs from the system (for example after a stock count). check the adjustment date and choose the responsible person . search and add each ingredient. enter the quantity and choose plus (add to stock) or minus (deduct from stock). note on minus adjustments: you cannot deduct more quantity than the current available stock. if a minus quantity exceeds current inventory, the system blocks the adjustment with the error: \"adjustment quantity exceeds available stock for [ingredient name].\" write the reason and click submit . saved adjustments are in stock > list stock adjustment . spoiled or thrown-away stock is recorded under waste & preserve instead (below), so it shows in the waste report. waste & preserve record waste & preserve > add waste & preserve choose the responsible person and the item type . there is no reason list; write any explanation in the note . production food menu : leftovers of a production. meal time and production date are required. enter waste qty and preserve qty ; together they cannot be more than what is left of the production. waste is only recorded; preserve qty is added back to food menu stock. preserve food menu : waste of food that was preserved earlier and is in food menu stock. pick the food menus yourself; only waste qty is entered, and it is taken out of food menu stock. a menu with no stock is refused (\"… has no stock in food menu stock.\"). ingredient : spoiled or expired raw ingredients. enter waste qty and loss amount . waste qty cannot be more than the current stock. item : wasted items. same fields and rule as ingredient. click submit , or save draft to finish later. only submitted records change stock. list waste & preserve shows active (submitted) or draft records. figure 9.3: add waste & preserve before the item type is chosen. common messages message why it happens what to do \"adjustment quantity exceeds available stock for [ingredient].\" you selected minus consumption status for a quantity greater than current on-hand stock. check physical counts and adjust the minus quantity so it does not exceed current stock. \"… has no stock in food menu stock.\" you tried to log waste on a preserved food menu that has 0 preserved quantity. check the food menu stock list under production before logging waste against preserved food. "}, {"title": "Purchases & Suppliers", "url": "20-purchases-suppliers.html", "category": "Kitchen & Stock", "roles": "Storekeeper, Accountant", "snippet": "Suppliers, purchases, returns, supplier payments, supplier advance and expenses.", "keywords": "purchase supplier return payment advance expense suppliers supplier &gt; add supplier buying stock purchase &gt; purchase forecast purchase &gt; add purchase pay what you owe: supplier payment &gt; add supplier payment supplier advance &gt; add supplier advance returning stock to a supplier purchase return &gt; add purchase return expenses expense &gt; add expense where saved records are", "text": " suppliers setup supplier > add supplier enter the supplier name , contact person , phone number , email and address. opening balance is what you already owe this supplier when you start. set the status and click submit . many suppliers can be added with bulk upload . buying stock optional purchase > purchase forecast works out which ingredients to buy for coming meal times, from past sales (or from the food menus' production amounts when there is no sales history) and the current stock . it never suggests less than an ingredient's minimum purchase qty . saved forecasts are in list purchase forecast . step 1 purchase > add purchase choose the supplier ( + adds a new one) and check the date . the reference no is filled in. under item , search and add each ingredient or item. enter the unit price and quantity ; the total is worked out. under payment details : add a discount if any (amount or %), check the g. total , choose the account you pay from and the paid amount. whatever is not paid shows as due and is owed to the supplier. if the supplier holds an advance from you, it can be used here as a payment. click submit , or save draft to finish later. figure 20.1: add purchase. step 2 pay what you owe: supplier payment > add supplier payment choose the supplier . the form shows the due amount and any advance amount . enter the pay amount , choose the payment method , add a note and click submit . advance supplier advance > add supplier advance money paid to a supplier before you buy. choose the supplier (the form shows the due amount and advance balance ), the type : payment (you pay the supplier) or refund (the supplier gives advance money back), the account and the amount . the advance can later pay part of a purchase. returning stock to a supplier return purchase return > add purchase return choose the supplier , then the purchase the goods came from (only active purchases are listed). check the return date . choose the status : taken by supplier money returned : the supplier gives credit at the return price . it first lowers what you still owe on that purchase; the rest is either refunded into a payment account ( refund to a payment account , choose the refund account ) or keep as supplier advance . taken by supplier product returned : the supplier replaces the same goods. taken by supplier product not returned : the supplier took the goods but has not settled yet. settle it later from list purchase return with settle (as money or as replacement). for each item enter the return quantity (and return price). write the reason for the return in the note and click submit . figure 20.2: add purchase return. expenses expense expense > add expense for money spent that is not stock (gas, cleaning, repairs). add categories first in add expense category . then choose the date , expense category , amount , the employee responsible, the payment method and an optional note (up to 500 characters). click submit . where saved records are supplier > list supplier , supplier payment > list supplier payment , supplier advance > list supplier advance . expense > list expense and expense > list expense category . purchase > list purchase and purchase return > list purchase return . "}, {"title": "Payment Accounts & Accounting", "url": "10-finance-accounting.html", "category": "Money & Staff", "roles": "Accountant, Owner", "snippet": "Payment accounts, deposits, transfers and what the accounting pages show.", "keywords": "payment account deposit withdraw transfer chart of accounts journal lock date payment accounts payment account &gt; add payment account deposits, withdrawals and transfers accounting accounting &gt; dashboard accounting &gt; chart of accounts accounting &gt; journal entries accounting &gt; accounting settings", "text": " payment accounts setup payment account > add payment account a payment account is a place money is kept or received: the cash drawer, a bank account, a card machine, mobile banking or an online payment service. every sale, purchase, expense and salary is paid from or into one of them. choose the account type : cash, bank, credit card, mobile banking, or an online service (paypal, stripe, razorpay, paystack, paytm, flutterwave, sslcommerz, senangpay, phonepe, myfatoorah). enter the title users will see, and the opening balance . for a bank add the bank name , branch name and account number (the account number must contain digits only ; letters or dashes will trigger \"the account number must contain digits only.\" ). for an online service, enter the keys from that service's account and the mode . for mobile banking you can choose a provider (bkash or nagad) to take online payments. click submit . figure 10.1: add payment account. more fields appear after the account type is chosen. all accounts are in payment account > list payment account . sorting payment accounts sets the order the active accounts are listed in. online payment keys & webhook addresses identified currency required : online payment gateways only work if your currency is recognized in settings > settings (see settings & white label ). webhook url appears after saving keys : for gateways that authenticate notifications (such as stripe, razorpay, and paypal), the copyable webhook url field only appears after the webhook secret key or webhook id is entered and saved. once saved, copy the displayed webhook url and paste it into the payment gateway developer console so the provider can confirm successful customer payments. money deposits, withdrawals and transfers add deposit or withdraw : the owner puts money into an account or takes it out. choose deposit or withdraw , the payment account , the amount and a note . add account transfer : move money between two accounts (for example drawer to bank). choose from and to , enter the amount ; the form shows each account's balance after the transfer. click submit transfer . saved records are in list deposit or withdraw and list account transfer . accounting you do not type accounting entries for daily work every sale, advance, refund, purchase, expense, salary and stock change writes its accounting entry by itself. for example, when you settle a cash bill, the cash account goes up and sales income goes up by the same amount. accountants use the pages below to check these entries. overview accounting > dashboard shows total revenue , total expenses , net profit , supplier payable and total receivables , a revenue & expenses chart, the expense breakdown , payment account balances, top expense categories and balance alerts . figure 10.2: accounting dashboard. accounts accounting > chart of accounts the list of all accounts in five groups: assets (what you own), liabilities (what you owe), equity (the owner's share), income and expenses . each row shows the opening and closing balance. figure 10.3: chart of accounts. entries accounting > journal entries every entry with its number, date, description, where it came from (pos sales, reservation, purchase …), the debit and credit amounts (always equal) and its status. filter by date. add journal entry is only for corrections an accountant makes by hand. figure 10.4: journal entries. control accounting > accounting settings lock date : nothing dated on or before this day can be posted, edited or reversed. clear it to reopen. fiscal year start month and go-live date . every change here is recorded in accounting audit log with the old and new value. the accounting reports (account statement, balance sheet, trial balance, transaction history, profit and loss, payment reconciliation, customer ledger, supplier ledger) are under accounting > reports . "}, {"title": "Accounting Reports & Ledgers", "url": "27-accounting-reports.html", "category": "Money & Staff", "roles": "Accountant, Owner", "snippet": "Trial balance, balance sheet, profit and loss, account statement, journals and audit log.", "keywords": "accounting trial balance balance sheet profit loss account statement journal audit log debit and credit in one minute every entry balances accounting &gt; reports account statement trial balance balance sheet profit and loss customer ledger and supplier ledger transaction history payment reconciliation accounting &gt; journal entries reading the list add journal entry (corrections only) undo a posted manual entry accounting &gt; accounting audit log who changed what what happens next common problems", "text": " before you start these pages are under accounting in the side menu. sales, purchases, expenses, salaries and stock already write their accounting entries by themselves; these pages let you read and check them. debit and credit in one minute basics every entry balances each entry has two sides that are always equal: debit and credit . a debit makes assets and expenses go up; a credit makes liabilities , equity and income go up. example: a guest pays 1,000 in cash for a buffet meal. your cash payment account is debited 1,000 (an asset goes up) and buffet sales revenue is credited 1,000 (income goes up). figure 27.1: account statement for one account: opening balance, total debit, total credit, closing balance and the running balance. accounting > reports 1 account statement use it to see every movement on one account. filters: select account , date from , date to , then submit . cards: opening balance , total debit , total credit , closing balance . then sn , date , voucher no. , description , module , debit , credit , running balance , and the closing balance . figure 27.2: trial balance: total debit, total credit, difference and check. 2 trial balance use it to check that total debits equal total credits. options: as of date, all account types (assets, liabilities, equity, income, expenses), hide zero balances . the fiscal year is shown. cards: total debit , total credit , difference , check ( balanced or unbalanced ). columns: code , account name , debit , credit . figure 27.3: balance sheet: assets on the left, liabilities & equity on the right. 3 balance sheet \"statement of financial position — assets = liabilities + equity\", on the as of date. assets (current assets, non-current assets) on one side; liabilities & equity (current liabilities, equity with retained earnings and current year earnings) on the other. cards: total assets , total liabilities + equity , check (balanced or unbalanced). figure 27.4: profit and loss for the chosen dates. 4 profit and loss filters: from date , to date , then filter ( reset filters clears them). sections: revenue , cost of goods sold (cogs) , gross profit , operating expenses , operating profit (ebit) , other income / expense , and net profit / (loss) with the net margin . 5–6 customer ledger and supplier ledger choose the customer ( select customer ) or supplier ( select supplier ), date from , date to , then submit . columns: sn , date , reference no. , description , module , debit , credit , running balance (the supplier ledger also shows account ). customer cards: total sales , payments received , customer advance , outstanding due . supplier cards: opening balance , total purchases , total payments , supplier advance , outstanding payable . figure 27.5: transaction history after submit. 7 transaction history filters: date from , date to , module , status (posted & reversed, posted, reversed, draft), account , search (journal no, reference). buttons: submit and reset filters . columns: sn , journal no. , date , reference , module , debit , credit , status , added by , added date , actions . a row opens to show its lines. 8 payment reconciliation use it to check that each payment account's cash book matches its account in the books. choose reconcile as of date and click filter . columns: sn , payment account , ledger account , cash book , ledger , difference , status ( reconciled or check ). when all match: \"every payment account's cash book agrees with its ledger account.\" otherwise: \"some payment accounts do not reconcile. the exceptions are listed under each account.\" the exceptions are \"cash rows with no journal entry\" and \"ledger lines with no cash row\". accounting > journal entries list reading the list filter with from date and to date and click filter . columns: sn , entry no , date , reference , source , debit , credit , status , posted by , actions . a row opens to show its lines . add add journal entry (corrections only) click add journal entry . enter the date and the narration (\"what this entry records and why\"). for each line choose the account , debit / credit , the amount , and if needed the customer or supplier and a line note . add line adds a line; remove line removes one. check that total debit equals total credit (the difference must be 0). click save & post , or save draft to finish later. a draft is opened from the list: edit draft , delete draft or post . entries cannot be dated on or before the lock date (\"the books are locked up to … entries must be dated after that day.\"). reverse undo a posted manual entry only a posted manual entry that is not itself a reversal has the reverse button. the reverse journal entry window says \"a new entry with every debit and credit swapped will be posted. the original stays in the ledger, marked reversed.\" enter the reason and, if needed, the reversal date (\"leave empty for today\"). click reverse . figure 27.6: accounting audit log after submit. accounting > accounting audit log audit who changed what filters: date from , date to , employee , module . click submit ( reset filters clears them). before you submit, the page says \"select filters and click submit to view the audit log.\" columns: sn , date & time , reference no , module name , action type (for example create, update, delete, auto journal posted, reverse entry), description , added by . what happens next reports only read the books; they change nothing. posting or reversing a journal entry changes account balances at once and is recorded in the accounting audit log. common problems message what to do trial balance shows unbalanced (\"debit and credit totals differ by …\") look at \"entries that do not balance:\" under it and correct them. payment reconciliation status check open the account's exceptions and fix the missing entry or cash row. \"the books are locked up to …\" date the entry after the lock date, or ask the accountant to change it in accounting settings. \"no go-live date is set, so only movements are compared (opening"}, {"title": "Fixed Assets", "url": "24-fixed-assets.html", "category": "Money & Staff", "roles": "Accountant, Owner", "snippet": "Fixed asset dashboard, categories, purchases, items, depreciation, maintenance and disposal.", "keywords": "asset fixed asset depreciation maintenance disposal category net book value fixed asset dashboard fixed asset &gt; dashboard asset categories fixed asset &gt; asset categories assets you already owned fixed asset &gt; add item buying new equipment (asset purchase) fixed asset &gt; add asset purchase posting monthly depreciation fixed asset &gt; depreciation maintenance fixed asset &gt; add maintenance disposal (selling or retiring an asset) fixed asset &gt; add disposal fixed asset settings fixed asset &gt; fixed asset settings fixed asset reports fixed asset &gt; fixed asset reports what happens next common problems", "text": " before you start fixed assets are things the restaurant owns and uses for years: kitchen equipment, furniture, freezers, computers. set up fixed asset settings and at least one entry in asset categories first. the accounts a category needs come from the chart of accounts. figure 24.1: fixed asset dashboard: the eight cards, book value by category and asset acquisitions. fixed asset dashboard overview fixed asset > dashboard choose a category under all categories and a period with from date and to date . the cards show: total assets : number of active assets. acquisition cost , accumulated depreciation and net book value (cost minus accumulated depreciation) of the active assets. this month's depreciation . maintenance cost in the chosen period. maintenance due : assets whose next maintenance date is within the next 7 days or already passed. disposed assets : number of disposed assets. charts: book value by category , depreciation trend , maintenance cost trend and asset acquisitions (last 12 months). asset categories setup fixed asset > asset categories click add category , fill in the form and click save . field required? what to enter example name yes the group of assets. kitchen equipment code yes a short code; each category needs its own. kit parent category no a bigger group this one belongs to. equipment asset account yes the account that holds these assets' cost (a non-current assets account). kitchen equipment accumulated depreciation yes the account that collects their depreciation. accumulated depreciation depreciation expense account yes the expense account for depreciation. depreciation expense depreciation method yes straight line or declining balance . straight line useful life (months) yes 1 to 600 months. 60 salvage value (%) no 0 to 100: what is left at the end, as a % of cost. 5 description no notes. stoves and ovens status yes active or inactive . active when you choose a category on an asset, its depreciation method and useful life (months) are copied to the asset, and the salvage value is worked out from its percentage if you have not entered one. assets you already owned add item fixed asset > add item the form opens with the note \"use this form for assets you already owned before the go-live date. buy new assets through asset purchase.\" for equipment you buy now, use fixed asset > add asset purchase instead. figure 24.2: add item with the go-live note and a category chosen. field required? what to enter example name yes what the asset is. gas range, 4 burners code yes filled in for you (from the asset code prefix); each asset needs its own. fa-0001 asset category yes its category. kitchen equipment brand , model , serial number , barcode / qr code no from the label on the equipment. — condition no new, good, fair or poor. good quantity yes a whole number, 1 or more. 1 purchase date yes when it was bought; not in the future. — available-for-use date yes when it was first used; not before the purchase date. — invoice no. no the supplier's invoice number. — purchase cost yes the price, more than 0. 120,000 additional capitalizable costs no delivery or installation. 10,000 total capitalized cost — worked out: purchase cost + additional capitalizable costs. 130,000 depreciation method , useful life (months) yes copied from the category; you can change them. straight line, 60 salvage value no what it is worth at the end of its life. 6,500 depreciation start date no \"optional. depreciation starts the month after the asset is put into use.\" — depreciation to go-live no depreciation the asset already had before the go-live date. shown only when the purchase date is before the go-live date (or no go-live date is set). 24,700 assigned employee no who looks after it. — note no up to 500 characters. — status yes active or inactive. active click submit . all assets are in fixed asset > list item . once depreciation has been posted for an asset, the form says \"depreciation is already posted for this asset; its cost and depreciation settings can no longer change.\" buying new equipment (asset purchase) purchase fixed asset > add asset purchase use this for equipment you buy now. saved purchases are in fixed asset > list asset purchases . figure 24.3: add asset purchase with the supplier chosen, one asset line and payment details. choose the supplier and check the date . enter the invoice no. if you have one. for each asset fill in a line: asset category , asset name , unit price and quantity (a whole number). the total is worked out. turn on track each unit to keep each unit as a separate asset. click add asset for another line. if a unit price is below the capitalization threshold in fixed asset settings, the line shows \"below the capitalization threshold: consider recording it as an expense.\" under payment details : enter a discount if any (amount or %), check the g. total , choose the account you pay from and the paid amount. what is not paid shows as due and is owed to the supplier. click submit , or save as draft to finish later. posting monthly depreciation depreciation fixed asset > depreciation depreciation spreads an asset's cost over its useful life. post it once a month. figure 24.4: depreciation for a month: the charge table, skipped assets and posted months. choose the month . the table shows each asset to charge: code , asset , category , accumulated before , charge and book value after . a charge that covers earlier months that were never posted shows \"includes catch-up for n months\". depreciation starts the month after the asset's available-for-use date . assets that are not charged are listed under skipped assets (click it to open the list), each with its reason: not set up, not in use yet, already charged, useful life ended or fully depreciated. click post depreciation . the month appears under posted months . to undo a month, click reverse on it under posted months , write the reason and click reverse . only the latest posted month can be reversed. maintenance m"}, {"title": "Staff, Roles & Salary", "url": "11-staff-payroll.html", "category": "Money & Staff", "roles": "Owner, Manager", "snippet": "Roles and permissions, employees, attendance and salary.", "keywords": "role permission employee designation attendance check-in salary roles and permissions roles &amp; permissions &gt; add role employees employee &gt; add employee attendance attendance salary salary &gt; add salary where saved records are", "text": " roles and permissions step 1 roles & permissions > add role enter the role name (for example cashier) and an optional description . under role permissions , tick what this role may do. permissions are grouped by area (dashboard, sales & pos, reservation …). the heading shows how many are ticked; select all ticks everything. click submit . you can only give permissions you have yourself. users only see the menus and buttons their role allows. figure 11.1: add role. employees step 2 employee > add employee add the job titles first in employee > add designation . then in add employee enter the first name , last name , phone number , designation and salary . if the person uses buffet erp, set will login? to yes and fill in the role , email address , password and, for quick login, the login pin (6 digits; generate makes one). each pin must be different. figure 11.2: list employee. the admin employee record the system includes a permanent admin employee record created during initial setup: cannot be deleted : the admin employee cannot be deleted from the system (attempting to delete it shows \"the admin employee cannot be deleted.\" ). must stay active : the admin account must always remain active so administrators cannot accidentally lock themselves out ( \"the admin employee must stay active.\" ). the admin employee : the admin's photo and password are not changed on edit employee. the screen says \"the admin changes their photo and password from change profile and change password in the profile menu.\" (see everyday basics ). editing permissions : only an admin user can modify the admin employee record ( \"only an admin can change the admin employee record.\" ). attendance daily attendance check-in / check-out : today's view of all active employees, with present today , absent today and who is checked in or checked out . add attendance : enter it by hand. choose the employee and date , the in time and out time (tick \"out time is next day (overnight)\" for night shifts), and an optional note . list attendance : all records with the time worked. figure 11.3: list attendance. salary monthly salary > add salary choose the salary month and salary year , and the salary generation date . choose the employees and click generate employee list . each row shows the basic salary and present / absent days. enter any bonus or deduct amount. the net salary and the total payable amount are worked out. under payment method , choose the account the money is paid from and the amount , add a note , and click submit . \"no employees available for salary generation this month.\" means everyone already has a salary for that month. where saved records are roles & permissions > role list , employee > list designation , employee > list employee , attendance > list attendance , salary > list salary . "}, {"title": "Which Report Do I Need?", "url": "22-reports-guide.html", "category": "Money & Staff", "roles": "Owner, Manager, Accountant", "snippet": "Every report screen and the question it answers.", "keywords": "report z report sales tax waste stock sales and the day reservations and customers kitchen and stock purchases, staff and assets", "text": " how reports work all reports are under report in the side menu. choose the filters (usually a date range) and click submit ; reset filters clears them. most reports can be printed or saved as pdf or excel. you only see the reports your role allows. sales and the day question report how did a day go: sales, money in and money out? daily summary report what was the end-of-day total for one date? z report what did each register take, per payment account? register report what did we sell each day? daily sale report which bills, with every line? detailed sale report how many guests (adults, children, seniors) came? guest report which paid extras sold best? add-on item sales report how much tax did we collect? tax report how much discount did we give, and which promotions? discount & promotion report what refunds were paid? refund report did we make a profit? profit loss report reservations and customers question report which bookings did we have? reservation report who cancelled or did not come, and what fee was kept? no-show & cancellation report who are our customers and what did they spend? customer report what does one customer owe or have paid? customer ledger report how many loyalty points do customers hold, and how many were used? available loyalty point report , usage loyalty point report which marketing messages were sent? marketing report which quotations were made? quotation report kitchen and stock question report what was cooked? production report how fast did the kitchen cook and answer refills? kitchen & refill performance how much of each ingredient was used? ingredient consumption report how much stock do we have, and what is low? stock report , low stock report how much cooked food is in stock? food menu stock report what does each dish cost to make? food menu cost report what was thrown away, and what was kept? waste report , preserve report purchases, staff and assets question report what did we buy? purchase report what did we spend on expenses? expense report how much do we owe each supplier? supplier due report , supplier ledger report what salaries were paid? employee salary report who came to work, and when? attendance report what fixed assets do we own? fixed asset report accounting reports balance sheet, trial balance, profit and loss, account statement, transaction history, payment reconciliation and the customer and supplier ledgers are under accounting > reports , not under report. "}, {"title": "Restaurant Setup Checklist", "url": "21-restaurant-setup.html", "category": "Setup", "roles": "Owner, Admin", "snippet": "Counters, floors, tables, printers, denominations, weekend and special days.", "keywords": "counter area floor table printer denomination weekend special day online reservation setting website settings &gt; online reservation setting sms, email &amp; whatsapp settings settings &gt; sms setting settings &gt; email settings settings &gt; whatsapp settings", "text": " do it in this order each step uses what the step before created. all pages are under settings unless another menu is named. # page what to enter 1 settings and white label restaurant name, currency, time zone, logos. see settings, tax & white label . 2 tax setting your tax rates, if you collect tax. 3 payment account > add payment account at least a cash account. see payment accounts & accounting . 4 add printer receipt and kitchen printers. see equipment & printers . 5 add area/floor area/floor name (for example \"1st floor\"), description, status. 6 add table table name , the area/floor , seat capacity , status. 7 floor/area plan design place the tables as they stand in the room and click save setting . 8 add counter counter name , the area/floor it serves (its floor plan is shown on that counter's pos), the invoice printer and bill printer , status. 9 add denomination optional. a list of the notes and coins of your currency ( amount , description, status). no other screen uses this list at the moment; closing the register does not ask you to count notes. 10 add meal time , weekend setting , add special day meal times and their prices. see how to set meal times & prices . 11 items menu units, ingredient categories, ingredients, food menu categories and food menus. see ingredients and food menus . 12 kitchen > add kitchen each kitchen, its printer and its food menu categories. see production & kitchen panel . 13 roles & permissions , employee roles, designations and user logins. see staff, roles & salary . 14 promotion & discount optional discounts and manager pins. see customers, promotions & loyalty . 15 website settings > online reservation setting optional public booking page (below). 16 sms setting , email settings , whatsapp settings optional, for messages to customers. saved records are in settings > list area/floor , list table , list counter , list denomination , list printer and list meal time . online website settings > online reservation setting general settings : the page heading, description, button text (for example \"reserve now\") and background image (1920×600 px recommended). online payment : which payment accounts guests can pay with, and the payment time limit (minutes) . an online booking that is not paid in this time expires. contact information and footer setting : shown on the public page. seo : the title, description and keywords search engines show. who will be notified after an online reservation : the users who get a notification. online reservation link : the address of your public booking page. click copy to share it. sms, email & whatsapp settings sms settings > sms setting choose the sms service provider : twilio, nexmo (vonage), provider (generic gateway), msg91, infobip, gupshup, smsgatewayhub, kaleyra, mimsms, bulk sms bd or mobishastra. fill in the fields that appear for that provider, from your account with them (for twilio: sid , token and twilio number ). set status to active and click submit . to test, open test sms , choose the country code , enter the number and message , and click send test sms . until a provider is set, sms screens show \"please enable and configure sms service provider first.\" email settings > email settings on configure mail , choose the mail type : smtp, mailgun, sendgrid, amazon ses, postmark, elastic email or sendinblue (brevo). fill in the fields for that type. for smtp: host address , mail port , encryption , mail username , mail password , mail from and mail from name . the other types ask for their key (for example api key or server token ) and the sender. set status and click submit . to test, open test mail , enter the email address , subject and message , and click send test email . whatsapp settings > whatsapp settings choose the whatsapp service provider : twilio, rcsoft, or disable. for twilio enter the account sid , auth token and twilio number . for rcsoft enter the app key and auth key . click submit . to test, open test whatsapp message , enter the number (with country code) and message , and click send whatsapp message . "}, {"title": "Settings, Tax & White Label", "url": "12-settings-branding.html", "category": "Setup", "roles": "Owner, Admin", "snippet": "Restaurant settings, tax, white label and the floor plan designer.", "keywords": "settings tax white label logo floor plan settings &gt; settings settings &gt; tax setting settings &gt; white label settings &gt; floor/area plan design", "text": " settings settings > settings the main restaurant settings. fields marked * are required. field what it does restaurant name , restaurant short name , website , invoice logo , invoice footer shown on invoices and receipts. date format , time zone how dates and times are shown. currency symbol , currency position , precision , decimals separator , thousands separator how money is displayed everywhere. important for online payments: online payments need to know your currency. these currency symbols are recognised: ৳ and tk (bdt), $ (usd), € (eur), £ (gbp), ₹ (inr), ₦ (ngn), ₵ (ghs), ₩ (krw), ฿ (thb), ₱ (php), ₫ (vnd), ₺ (try), ₽ (rub), rm (myr), rp (idr), r$ (brl), s$ (sgd), a$ (aud), c$ (cad), hk$ (hkd), nz$ (nzd), mx$ (mxn), ksh (kes), د.إ (aed), ر.س (sar), د.ك (kwd), ر.ق (qar). for any other currency, type its 3-letter code (for example usd) as the currency symbol. otherwise settings shows \"the currency cannot be identified from the saved currency symbol. enter your currency code (e.g. usd) to enable online payments.\" default customer , default payment method picked automatically in forms. login option , active login button which login methods (email, pin or both) are offered and which tab opens first. order number full order number or short order number on invoices. sms send auto(in final invoice) send an sms to the customer when the bill is settled. loyalty point , loyalty point rate , minimum loyalty point to redeem turn loyalty points on and set their value (see customers, promotions & loyalty ). wastage penalty , wastage penalty amount a charge per plate with too much leftover food, added at billing. no-show & cancellation fee the part of an advance kept when a booking is cancelled or a guest does not come: an amount or a %. figure 12.1: settings > settings. reset transactional data this red button deletes all sales, purchases, waste records, expenses, supplier due payments and customer receivables. it cannot be undone. use it only when you start fresh after testing. tax settings > tax setting turn collect tax on, enter your tax registration number , and add each tax with add tax rate (name and rate). taxes can be grouped with assign sub taxes . for india, my tax is gst and indian state selection apply gst by state. the tax shows on bills as its own line. brand settings > white label set the site title , footer text , primary color and secondary color , the white site logo , the dark mode site logo and the favicon (the small browser-tab icon). click submit . the name and logo you set here are what staff see, so they may differ from \"buffet erp\". figure 12.2: white label. floor settings > floor/area plan design choose the area/floor and drag its tables into place as they stand in your dining room. add zones ( add zone ), pictures, drawings and text, rotate with rotate left / rotate right , pick a background, and click save setting . this layout is the floor plan shown on the pos and in add reservation. tables are added first in settings > add table . figure 12.3: floor/area plan design. "}, {"title": "How to Set Meal Times & Prices", "url": "13-howto-meal-pricing.html", "category": "Setup", "roles": "Owner, Manager", "snippet": "Create meal times with adult, child and senior prices and weekend or special day prices.", "keywords": "meal time price weekend special day advance settings &gt; add meal time check settings &gt; list meal time settings &gt; weekend setting settings &gt; add special day", "text": " three kinds of price each meal time has normal prices. weekend setting gives the same meal times their own prices on the days you mark as weekend, and a special day (for example eid or new year) gives them their own prices on one date. these are separate prices you type in, not a percentage added to the normal price. step 1 settings > add meal time field required? what to enter meal name yes for example breakfast, lunch, dinner. start time / end time yes when the meal time runs. total time is worked out. cost per person (adult) , (senior) , (child) yes the price per guest of each kind. who counts as a child or senior is your restaurant's own rule. advance payment amount yes the minimum advance for a booking: an amount per guest (for example 20) or a % of the booking (for example 10%). loyalty point when loyalty is on points a customer earns when a reservation for this meal time is settled at the pos. description , status status: yes only active meal times are used. click submit . figure 13.1: add meal time. step 2 check settings > list meal time the list shows each meal time with its times, the three prices and the advance. figure 13.2: list meal time. step 3 settings > weekend setting tick the weekend days . for each meal time enter the weekend cost per person (adult, senior, child) and advance payment amount . click submit . figure 13.3: weekend setting. step 4 settings > add special day enter the special day name (for example eid) and the date . for each meal time enter the prices and advance payment amount for that day. set the status and click submit . list special day shows them all. after changing prices food menus also have production amounts for weekend days and special days ( food menus & recipes ). fill them in after you add weekend days or a special day. "}, {"title": "How to Seat & Bill a Walk-In", "url": "14-howto-walkin-dining.html", "category": "How-To Guides", "roles": "Cashier", "snippet": "Instant Reservation, check-in with tokens, then Generate invoice and Settle & close.", "keywords": "walk in instant reservation check in settle click instant reservation enter the guest and the head count check in and print tokens bill the guests if something is different", "text": " before you start you need an open register (if not, sale > pos sends you to open register ), a running meal time, and paper in the receipt printer. step 1 click instant reservation open sale > pos . in the left panel click instant reservation . step 2 enter the guest and the head count field required? what to enter search customer no find a saved customer by name or phone. otherwise fill in the fields below. customer name yes the guest's name. phone number yes 4 to 15 digits, with the country code. adults / children / senior at least 1 guest use + and −. walk-in guest (advance pay optional) — tick it when you take no money now. click create reservation . the new reservation is selected in the right panel. figure 14.1: instant reservation. step 3 check in and print tokens in the right panel under guests arriving now , enter the guests who are here. optional: click choose table and tap free tables on the floor plan (the chosen seats turn yellow). set guests per table if you use more than one table. click check in n & print n tokens (or check in n ), then print n slips . hand the tokens to the guests. the checked-in guests' seats now show red (reserved). step 4 bill the guests select the party under in house (or tap their table). click generate invoice . apply a discount if the guest has one, choose the payment method and amount (the screen shows the change to return for cash). click settle & close . the party moves to the settled tab. the table shows cleaning ; click mark ready when it is reset. if something is different situation what to do the group is bigger than one table in choose table tap two or more free tables and set guests per table. guests want to pay separately in the invoice use split bill (2 ways or more) and take each share's payment. more guests come later select the reservation again and check them in under guests arriving now . "}, {"title": "How to Request Refills & Log Waste", "url": "15-howto-kitchen-refills.html", "category": "How-To Guides", "roles": "Cashier, Chef", "snippet": "Send a refill from the POS, mark it refilled in the kitchen, record leftovers.", "keywords": "refill waste preserve cashier: send the refill kitchen: refill and mark it after the meal time: record leftovers", "text": " before you start only food menus marked is refillable? = yes can be requested, and their category must be linked to a kitchen. otherwise the pos shows \"no refillable food items…\" or \"no kitchen assigned\". step 1 cashier: send the refill on the pos top bar click refill . the refill buffet window opens. tap the dishes that are running low. add a note for kitchen (optional) . click send to kitchen . you get a notification when the kitchen marks it done. figure 15.1: the refill buffet window. step 2 kitchen: refill and mark it the kitchen panel plays a sound and the refill request button shows how many requests are waiting. tap refill request to see the requests for your kitchen. refill the dish, then tap mark refilled (or mark all refilled ). a request shows completed once every kitchen has refilled its part. figure 15.2: refill request view on the kitchen panel (no requests waiting). step 3 after the meal time: record leftovers in production > list production , set the meal time status of the production to done and confirm. click add waste & preserve (or open waste & preserve > add waste & preserve and choose production food menu , the meal time and production date). for each dish enter the waste qty (thrown away) and preserve qty (kept for a later meal; it goes back to food menu stock). click submit (or save draft ). to throw away preserved food later, use the type preserve food menu . see ingredients, stock & waste for all four types. "}, {"title": "How to Close the Register", "url": "16-howto-shift-closing.html", "category": "How-To Guides", "roles": "Cashier", "snippet": "Check the register totals, print an X-report, close the register, view the Z Report.", "keywords": "close register x-report z report check the register totals print an x-report (optional) close the register view the z report (manager)", "text": " before you start settle the bills of guests who have finished. closing the register is only a confirmation: there is no money counting step in buffet erp. step 1 check the register totals on the pos top bar click register . the register details window shows your counter, the time range, and for each payment account: opening balance (+) , purchase (-) , sale (+) , reservation advance (+) due receive (+) , due payment (-) , expense (-) , refund amount (-) closing balance : what should be in that account now. you can print it or export it to excel, csv or pdf. figure 16.1: register details. close register is at the bottom left. step 2 print an x-report (optional) click shift summary on the pos top bar, then print x-report . it shows the totals for this meal time so far (guests, sales, discounts, bills and money per payment account). printing it does not close the shift or the register. figure 16.2: shift summary. step 3 close the register in register details click close register . the question \"close the register on [counter]? you will need to open or join a register again to use the pos.\" appears. click confirm . \"register closed\" appears and you are taken to the open register page. step 4 view the z report (manager) the z report is a separate report page; closing the register does not print it. open report > z report , pick the date and click submit . print it, or save it as pdf or excel. situation what to do the money in the drawer differs from the closing balance look for payments made from the drawer that were not entered. record a missing expense in expense > add expense . another cashier takes over the counter do not close the register. the next cashier joins it on open register > existing register . "}, {"title": "Troubleshooting & FAQ", "url": "17-troubleshooting-faq.html", "category": "Help", "roles": "All users", "snippet": "Common messages and what to do about them.", "keywords": "error message problem pin register 1. i see \"no open register found. please open a register first.\" 2. what is the difference between the 6-digit pin and the 4-digit pin? 3. the kitchen panel says \"kitchen id is missing.\" 4. more guests came than were booked. 5. the online booking page rejected the guest's answer. 6. a dish is missing from the refill window. 7. the receipt printer does not print. 8. i cannot see a menu or button that a colleague has. 9. \"you cannot submit this production because the following ingredients are out of stock or not enough stock\"", "text": " 1. i see \"no open register found. please open a register first.\" the pos only works while you have an open register, so it sends you to open register . open a new register for your counter, or join one that is already open ( existing register ), then go back to sale > pos . if you had a register open, it may have been closed with close register . 2. what is the difference between the 6-digit pin and the 4-digit pin? 6-digit login pin : signs you in on the login using pin tab. a manager sets it on your employee record. 4-digit discount pin : approves a manual discount at the pos. it is set per approver on a manual discount promotion in promotion & discount . 3. the kitchen panel says \"kitchen id is missing.\" the panel was opened without choosing a kitchen. open kitchen > list kitchen and click the icon in the panel column of your kitchen. 4. more guests came than were booked. select the booking at the pos and enter the real number under guests arriving now . the extra guests are charged at the per-person price; the advance already paid is taken off the bill. 5. the online booking page rejected the guest's answer. the page asks a small sum (for example 7 + 5) to stop spam bookings. the guest must type the correct answer before continuing. 6. a dish is missing from the refill window. only food menus with is refillable? = yes are listed, and the dish's category must be linked to a kitchen (\"no kitchen assigned\" otherwise). fix it in the food menu or in kitchen > list kitchen . 7. the receipt printer does not print. check that the printer is on and has paper. in settings > list printer check the printer's details: for a network printer the ip address and port (usually 9100), for a windows printer the share name. print a test page from the printer to see its ip address and port. 8. i cannot see a menu or button that a colleague has. your role does not include that permission. ask a manager to change the role in roles & permissions . 9. \"you cannot submit this production because the following ingredients are out of stock or not enough stock\" buy the missing ingredients ( purchase > add purchase ), correct the stock ( stock > add stock adjustment ), or lower the production quantities. "}, {"title": "Glossary", "url": "18-glossary.html", "category": "Help", "roles": "All users", "snippet": "Plain-language meaning of the words used in Buffet ERP.", "keywords": "glossary terms", "text": " word meaning in buffet erp meal time a buffet session such as lunch, with a start and end time and its own prices. per-person price the price for each adult, child or senior guest for a meal time. weekend / special day price separate prices used on weekend days or on a special date instead of the normal meal time price. reservation a booking for a date and meal time. walk-ins also get one, through instant reservation. advance money paid before the meal. it is taken off the final bill. check in recording the guests who have arrived, at the pos. in house guests who are checked in and still dining. no-show a booking whose guests did not come. it is cancelled; a fee may be kept from the advance. food token a slip printed for each guest for a token food (for example seafood or ice cream), handed in at the food counter. add-on a paid extra (drink or dish) added to the bill. refill request a message from the pos to the kitchen that a buffet dish is running low. register a cashier session on a counter, from open register to close register, with an opening balance per payment account. counter a cashier station, linked to a floor and its printers. x-report a print of the current meal time's totals. it closes nothing. z report the end-of-day report for a chosen date, under report > z report. production a cooking plan for one meal time: which food menus and how much. food menu stock cooked food in stock, in production units (for example portions). kot (kitchen order ticket) a printed list of what a kitchen has to cook for a production. kitchen panel the kitchen's screen with items to cook and refill requests. waste food or stock thrown away, recorded so the loss is known. preserve leftover cooked food kept for a later meal; it goes back into food menu stock. payment account where money is kept or received: cash drawer, bank, card, mobile banking or an online service. supplier advance money paid to a supplier before buying; it can be used to pay a later purchase. debit / credit the two sides of every accounting entry. they are always equal. buffet erp writes them for you. journal entry one accounting record with its debits and credits. chart of accounts the list of all accounts: assets, liabilities, equity, income and expenses. lock date nothing dated on or before it can be changed in the accounts. white label your own name, colours and logos shown instead of the default ones. "}];
